      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Most events I’ve been to that suggest or request “poor or better” still don’t end up contacting or removing people for being very poor because they’re not actually over whatever specific internal limits the group is actually monitoring for.\n\nIt would be much more robust if a group could specify what kinds of avatar limits they don’t want to allow. As-is, I can see many group hosts ignoring this feature addition because it blocks more people than they would want to.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
